# The login screen, a wrong password, a good login to the home screen
# (a Ctrl key typed in the middle of the password ignored), and
# quitting, refused; after logging out, F3 on the password leaves the
# program as Esc does, so the snapshot after it is never taken.  Also
# run with BIOS output and with CGA snow avoidance, against the same
# goldens.
#@ BIOS
#@ SNOW
S LOGIN
T ADMIN
K ENTER
T wrong
K ENTER
S BADPW
T Retro
K CTRL-S
T 1986
K ENTER
S HOME
K F3
S QUIT
T N
K ALT-O
T L
T ADMIN
K ENTER F3
S STAYED
